{
  "_comment": "OPTIONAL purple-sparrow backend for dronAIcharya. This file is an EXAMPLE and is NOT loaded automatically — dronAIcharya works fully without any backend. Wire it in only if you want to learn/build against a real agent-native backend. The `setup` skill walks you through it.",
  "_how_to_use": [
    "1. Clone and build purple-sparrow (Go): CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o purplesparrow ./cmd/purplesparrow  (from github.com/dibakshya01/purple-sparrow)",
    "2. Run the backend:  PS_ADMIN_API_KEY=ps_sk_dev ./purplesparrow   (serves HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8787)",
    "3. Register this MCP server with YOUR key. Easiest: `claude mcp add` at user scope, OR copy the server block below into your own MCP config and replace <your-api-key>.",
    "4. purplesparrow must be on your PATH (or use an absolute path in 'command'). The HTTP backend (step 2) must be running for the MCP tools to work.",
    "5. In your dronAIcharya journey, set flags.purpleSparrow=true in ./.dronacharya/progress.json .",
    "NOTE: purple-sparrow is alpha and its policy engine 'needs an independent security audit before regulated data' — great for learning, not for real/regulated data."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "purple-sparrow": {
      "command": "purplesparrow",
      "args": ["mcp"],
      "env": {
        "PS_API_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8787",
        "PS_API_KEY": "<your-api-key>"
      }
    }
  }
}
